      "message": "Question for reviewers: should this pre-allocation drain only record OOM?\n\nAs written, any non-OOM error found here sets the sticky backend error flag (see getErrorAndCheckForOOM()). But an error drained *before* the allocation can\u0027t have come from the allocation. It is left over from an earlier GL call: either a client\u0027s raw GL on this context, or a Skia draw whose error we didn\u0027t check because command checks are off.\n\nOptions:\n1. Keep as is: record everything. Fails closed, but a stale error can fail an unrelated write.\n2. Record only OOM here (OOM still sets oomed()); only the post-call check records non-OOM errors. Errors are attributed to the operation that caused them. Non-OOM errors from earlier unchecked draws get dropped, which matches clients having turned command checks off.\n\nI lean toward 2. Thoughts?",
